Aegis-V (15-early-tools README): install calls chown (path, -1, -1) when
neither -o nor -g is given. Linux takes -1 as "no change"; Tilck's
vfs_chown() accepts only owner 0 and group 0 and returns EPERM, so every
install would fail. Skip chown when there is nothing to change, as
lib/makepath.c already does (and as later coreutils' install does).

--- coreutils-5.0/src/install.c
+++ coreutils-5.0/src/install.c
@@ -462,7 +462,8 @@
      want to know.  But AFS returns EPERM when you try to change a
      file's group; thus the kludge.  */
 
-  if (chown (path, owner_id, group_id)
+  if ((owner_id != (uid_t) -1 || group_id != (gid_t) -1)
+      && chown (path, owner_id, group_id)
 #ifdef AFS
       && errno != EPERM
 #endif
